<title>USA: SEC votes to send mutual fund reforms for comment.</title>
<headline>SEC votes to send mutual fund reforms for comment.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Commission Thursday voted 4-0 to send mutual fund reform proposals out for 90-day public comment.</p>
<p>&quot;Today's proposals represent the most sweeping revision of mutual fund disclosure in 14 years,&quot; SEC Chairman Arthur Levitt said at the commission's opening meeting.</p>
<p>The proposals will respond to investors' concerns and will help them evaluate whether a particular fund is right for them, Levitt said.</p>
</text>
